# PinchKey device access.
#
# Two rules are needed, and the second is the one that is easy to miss:
#
#   1. /dev/input/event*  — SUBSYSTEM=="input"  — to read real devices
#   2. /dev/uinput        — SUBSYSTEM=="misc"   — to create virtual ones
#
# A rule matching only KERNEL=="event*", SUBSYSTEM=="input" never touches
# /dev/uinput, which ships as 0600 root:root. Without rule 2 the daemon
# cannot create its virtual touchpad except as root.

KERNEL=="event*", SUBSYSTEM=="input", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc",  GROUP="input", MODE="0660", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
